---
// Download cards (#517). Static: /download.js (public/) fills each platform from its manifest
// in /updates/ (windows.json, android.json, linux.json, written by the release scripts); a card
// stays hidden until its manifest is online. The script also puts the visitor's system first
// and marks it (#48). The steps live in the installation guide, not here. External script:
// the server's CSP forbids inline code.
---

<div class="sg-downloads not-content" id="downloads">
  <section class="sg-platform" id="windows" aria-labelledby="windows-title" hidden>
    <div class="sg-platform-head">
      <h2 id="windows-title">Windows</h2>
      <span class="sg-badge" hidden>Your system</span>
    </div>
    <a class="sg-button" id="windows-link" href="#">Download for Windows</a>
    <p class="sg-meta" id="windows-meta"></p>
    <p>
      Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, AVX2-capable processor. No administrator rights needed. Windows may
      warn about an unrecognised app the first time: see the{" "}
      <a href="/install/">installation guide</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-platform" id="android" aria-labelledby="android-title" hidden>
    <div class="sg-platform-head">
      <h2 id="android-title">Android</h2>
      <span class="sg-badge" hidden>Your system</span>
    </div>
    <a class="sg-button" id="android-link" href="#">Download for Android</a>
    <p class="sg-meta" id="android-meta"></p>
    <p>
      Android 7 or newer, 64-bit (ARM). The first time, allow your browser to install apps (<a
        href="/install/">installation guide</a>).
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="sg-platform" id="linux" aria-labelledby="linux-title" hidden>
    <div class="sg-platform-head">
      <h2 id="linux-title">Linux</h2>
      <span class="sg-badge" hidden>Your system</span>
    </div>
    <a class="sg-button" id="linux-link" href="#">Download the AppImage</a>
    <p class="sg-meta" id="linux-meta"></p>
    <p>
      64-bit (x86-64): Ubuntu 22.04, Debian 12, Fedora 36 or newer. Needs <strong>mpv</strong> and
      a desktop keyring: see the <a href="/install/">installation guide</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</div>

<p class="sg-meta" id="none" hidden>No version is available right now.</p>

<p class="sg-meta">Once installed, the app checks for new versions on its own.</p>

<section class="sg-notes not-content" id="notes-card" aria-labelledby="notes-title" hidden>
  <h2 id="notes-title">What's new</h2>
  <ul id="notes"></ul>
</section>

<script is:inline src="/download.js"></script>
